// A sub_process pack wields Haymaker: three turns of wind-up, the
// aim locked on the first, then one big hit. This is the HOSTILE half of
// the charge tuning, the half the bin can measure — the bin's party plays
// All-Attack and never invokes a routine, so it cannot throw the player's
// own Haymaker (the played arena screen does; see `charge-long-compile.ron`).
//
// `opponent_routines` is how a hostile gets a routine here: in play it comes
// only from the wild roll, never the species kit. Read the win rate against
// the same file with that row removed, in the same build — arena numbers
// compare within one build only.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 8, zone: 2),
    opponents: [(species: "sub_process", count: 2)],
    opponent_routines: ["haymaker"],
    model: Tactical,
    approach: Some(East),
    reps: 50,
    seed: 1,
)
